{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: have the measurement grammar produce numeric quantities and retire quantity.rs's re-parse",
  "description": "The measurement grammar (ingredient_parser/measure.rs) reads amounts and units from tokens but still returns strings (\"1 1/2\", \"2 to 3\", \"1/4 plus 1/8\", \"15-ounce can\"). ingredient_parser/quantity.rs then re-parses those strings with regexes: ranges, mixed numbers, \"plus\" compounds, package and per-item weights (\"15-ounce can\", \"8 oz. each\"), inch pieces, and weights stated in the note. \
The grammar already knows which tokens were a range, a mixed number or a package size, so it could emit quantity::Term values directly and keep the display strings only for display. \
That deletes the second grammar and the cases where the two disagree. \
Coordinate with p2-calorie-architecture (or its successors), which owns everything after the line is parsed. \
Expect no data/ diffs from the move itself; any change should be a nameable fix.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ingredient-parser",
    "ramekin-core",
  ],
